# Session handoff (mandatory)

## Two memory files — do not confuse them

| File | Purpose | When to update |
|------|---------|----------------|
| **`claude-current-remindifier-state.md`** | Living session snapshot: status, recent commits, agreements, in-progress work, user preferences | **End of every meaningful session** |
| **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`** | Stable architecture: routes, i18n, data layer, pitfalls | Only when conventions or structure change |

**Never** create ad-hoc context files (`AI_PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks.

## Session START (before any work)

1. Read **`claude-current-remindifier-state.md`**
2. Read **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`**
3. `git pull --rebase origin sandbox`

## Session END (after meaningful work)

1. Update **`claude-current-remindifier-state.md`**: latest commit, what was done, uncommitted changes, new user agreements
2. Update **`PROJECT_MEMORY.md`** only if architecture/routes/conventions changed
3. Stage, commit, **`git push origin sandbox`** (user rule: always push after task)
4. Do not commit: `.env`, `coverage/`, `expo-output.log`

## User agreements → always record in state file

New preferences (git workflow, UX choices, naming) go under **User Preferences** in `claude-current-remindifier-state.md`.

## Skill

For explicit memory updates, follow `.cursor/skills/project-memory/SKILL.md`.
